# Avoid Compatibility Wrappers

Do not add backward-compatibility wrappers, aliases, duplicate entry points, or
pass-through APIs in Shell or TypeScript by default.

Prefer one canonical implementation:

- Update all repository callers, documentation, tests, and package scripts.
- Remove obsolete names instead of forwarding them to the new name.
- Keep a wrapper only when an external contract requires it, such as a
  third-party callback signature, deployed interface, or explicitly requested
  user-facing compatibility.
- If compatibility may be required but the contract is unclear, ask before
  preserving the old entry point.
